<title>NETHERLANDS: Ceteco 1996 eps up 7 percent.</title>
<headline>Ceteco 1996 eps up 7 percent.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net per shr (guilders)	     3.72 vs   3.49</p>
<p>    Net profit			    28.1  vs  25.1</p>
<p>    Dividend (guilders)		  0.75 vs   0.70</p>
<p>    Turnover			     717    vs 482</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    84.6  vs  60.8</p>
<p>NOTE - Trading company and retailer Ceteco Holding NV is mainly active in Latin America. The company, in which Hagemeyer, owns a 70 percent stake said in August it expected sales and profits to grow in 1996.  </p>
<p>    Total operating costs	    202.5  vs 139.2</p>
<p>    Associates' income	charge   0.06 vs   0.4 charge</p>
<p>    Financial charges		   52.8  vs  30.2</p>
<p>    Tax				     3.0   vs   3.2</p>
<p>    Minorities' charge		   0.7  vs   2.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Ceteco said its 1996 dividend could be taken up either in cash or in new Ceteco shares. Details of the optional stock dividend will be published on April 8, 1997.</p>
<p>Hong Kong's First Pacific owns a controlling stake in Ceteco's parent Hagemeyer.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
